const HELP_ARTICLES = {
"adding-bleed-to-your-file": "<p>Add <strong>3 mm bleed</strong> on every side for commercial print (make your canvas 6 mm wider and 6 mm taller than the final size); for large-format work like panels, add <strong>10 mm</strong> on every side. Run background colours and images all the way to the edge.</p><ul><li><strong>InDesign / Illustrator:</strong> Document Setup → Bleed (3 mm commercial / 10 mm panels); export the PDF with \"Use document bleed settings\" ticked.</li><li><strong>Canva:</strong> File → \"Show print bleed\"; export as PDF Print with crop marks and bleed.</li></ul><p>Keep text and logos at least <strong>5 mm inside</strong> the final size — that's the safety margin. And please don't send Word documents — we don't accept them, because the layout tends to shift when they're converted to PDF.</p>",
"adding-elements-and-images": "<p><strong>How do I add elements, borders, etc?</strong></p><p>Click the elements tab from the side panel and use the search bar to look for specific elements. You can also browse all elements by clicking “See all”. Elements include shapes, lines, illustrations, icons, frames, grids, stickers, charts and gradients. If you want to add a border, simply follow the same process but search ‘borders’ in the search bar. </p><p><strong>How do I add images on Canva to my designs?</strong></p><p>From the editor side panel, click the “Photos” tab. To look for specific images just type keywords into the search bar or click suggested categories. To add an image to your design simply click on it. Images that you use will be grouped together under “Recently Used” on the “Photos” tab. You can use images as backgrounds by right clicking and click below to change the background.</p><p><strong>How do I upload my own images?</strong></p><p>You can upload your own images to use in your designs. From the editor side panel, click the tab “uploads”. Select and drag the image to upload it or click the “upload” button. Once it’s been uploaded you can click on the image to add it to your design. You can then easily resize your images, adjust their settings or apply special filters and effects all within Canva!</p><p>Still unsure? Check out Canva’s tutorials <a href=\"https://www.canva.com/designschool/tutorials/\">here</a>, or <a href=\"#new2contactform\">get in touch</a> with our customer service team who would be happy to help!</p>",
"can-i-cancel-my-order": "<p>Once payment has been made and the artwork is approved, your order will enter the production stage. Before reaching this stage, you have the option to cancel your order in your account at any time. Custom print orders that have been approved and are in production or have been dispatched cannot be cancelled or returned, since they were made according to your unique specifications.</p><h3><strong>How can I cancel my order?</strong></h3><ol><li>Go to the \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" page in \"My Account.\"</li><li><p>Click on the \"Order Information\" button for the relevant order you want to cancel.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-29e25cb070/bba36c6727eb6e741f51a4e204407641/29e25cb070-order-20detail-20butten-20uk-20site-uoe.png\" alt=\"order-20detail-20butten-20uk-20site-uoe.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li><p> When you have the order details, click on the \"Cancel Order\" button.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-c87e6a15cc/eb71e8360ceac1d2dc27695f73bea3a8/c87e6a15cc-cancel-20order-20button-20uk-5ni.png\" alt=\"cancel-20order-20button-20uk-5ni.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li>Select one of the cancellation reasons from the menu.</li><li><p>Click \"Yes, Cancel my Order.\"</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-35f56c15b2/db10ba07ba0c80dc2e57370436a93869/35f56c15b2-yes-20cancel-20my-20order-20button-20menu-mks.png\" alt=\"yes-20cancel-20my-20order-20button-20menu-mks.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li>You did it! By following these steps, you have successfully cancelled your order. </li></ol><p>To ensure that everything has been processed correctly, you will receive a confirmation email from us. You can also keep an eye on the \"Orders\" page to see if the status of your order has been successfully changed to \"Cancelled.\"</p><h3>What should I do if I want to cancel specific products, not my entire order?</h3><p>If you need to cancel a specific product from your order instead of the entire order, please get in touch with one of our <a href=\"#new2contactform\">print experts</a> for assistance. As long as the product has not yet entered the production stage, it is still possible to cancel it.</p>",
"can-i-change-my-default-delivery-address-that-is-used-for-all-orders": "<p>Manage and update your shipping addresses for future orders through your account's '<a href=\"#addresses\">My Addresses</a>' page. Access this page by hovering over your name in the top right corner of your screen and selecting 'My Addresses.'</p><h3><strong>Edit the default billing and shipping address:</strong></h3><ul><li>Click 'Edit Address' in the box labeled 'Standard Billing Address &amp; Default Delivery Address.'</li><li>Make any necessary changes.</li><li>Click 'Edit Address' to save your updates.</li></ul>",
"can-i-change-my-delivery-address-when-i-have-already-placed-my-order": "<p>Your address can still be changed if our production location hasn't generated your shipping label yet. </p><ol><li>Go to '<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>' in your account by hovering over your name in the top right of your screen.</li><li>Once you're on the order overview page, select the order for which you need to change the shipping address and click on 'Order Details.'</li><li>On this page, you can adjust the shipping address by clicking 'Edit Address' in the 'Delivery Address' field located on the right side of your screen.*</li><li>You have the option to edit your existing address by clicking the pencil icon, or you can add a new address by selecting 'Add New Address' in the lower right corner of the pop-up. Please note that these addresses will be added or updated in your address book for future orders.</li><li>After making your changes, click 'Confirm Address' to save the modifications.</li></ol><p><em>*****If 'edit address' is not showing up in your order page to change the address, this means that a shipping label is already made for your order and therefore your shipping address can't be changed anymore.</em></p>",
"can-i-change-my-delivery-address": "<p>Manage and update your shipping addresses for future orders through your account's '<a href=\"#addresses\">My Addresses</a>' page. Access this page by hovering over your name in the top right corner of your screen and selecting 'My Addresses.' On this page, you have three options for making changes:</p><h3><strong>1. Edit the default billing and shipping address:</strong></h3><ul><li>Click 'Edit Address' in the box labeled 'Standard Billing Address &amp; Default Delivery Address.'</li><li>Make any necessary changes.</li><li>Click 'Edit Address' to save your updates.</li></ul><h3><strong>2. Add a new address to your address book:</strong></h3><ul><li>Click the green 'Add Address' button.</li><li>Fill out the new address details.</li><li>Click 'Save Address' to add it to your address book.</li></ul><h3><strong>3. Edit a saved address in your address book:</strong></h3><ul><li>If you have multiple addresses in your address book, they will appear under 'My Saved Addresses' on the 'My Addresses' page, each with its own row. On the right side of each row, you will find three dots. Click on these dots.</li><li>Select 'Edit Address.'</li><li>Make the necessary changes. </li><li>Click 'Edit Address' to save your updates.</li></ul><p><em>Need to update the address for an existing order? Please refer to</em><a href=\"help-article.html?q=can-i-change-my-delivery-address-when-i-have-already-placed-my-order\"><em>this article</em></a><em>for more information!</em></p>",
"can-i-change-my-delivery-date": "<p>Did you choose the wrong delivery date and do we offer a quicker one online? You can <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and we can easily change your order and link the payments that were already made, as long as your order has not reached the production stage yet. We will send you a payment link to pay the remaining amount. </p><p>Please note that this only applies if your order is not in production!</p>",
"can-i-change-my-order": "<p>If your order is unpaid or the file(s) haven't been uploaded yet, you can still make changes. However, once the order enters production, modifications or cancellations are no longer possible. Once your order is paid for and the artwork is approved, it goes into production, and you can no longer make any modifications. </p><p>You can easily check the status of your order and make the following changes by visiting the '<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>' page in '<a href=\"#my-account\">My Account</a>'. </p><h2>How do I make changes to my order? </h2><p>There are several changes you can make to your order. </p><h4>I want to make changes to my file: </h4><ol><li>If you haven't reviewed your digital proof yet but you already know you want to make changes to your current file, you can open the upload and proof page and select the following button: 'there is a mistake in my file/ I would like to upload a new file'. This will lead you to a page where you can upload a new file. </li><li>If you have already approved the digital proof, you will find a button to 'change the submitted file(s)'. Clicking this button will lead you to a page where you can re-upload your files. </li></ol><h4>I want to change my address details:</h4><p>If you wish to change your shipping address, you can do this yourself before the payment and proofing. Simply go to the ' 'order'' page in ''My Account'' and select the order you wish to change the address to. The shipping address you chose for this order can be found at the top of this page, under the order number. Here you will find an 'edit' button. If you click on it, a pop up will show your address book. You can select an address that is already registered in your account, or you can create a new address. </p><h4>I want to change my billing address: </h4><p>If you wish to change the billing address of your order, please reach out to our customer experience team <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a>.</p><h3>I can not find any buttons any more on my page:</h3><p>This likely means you have already approved your artwork and paid for your order. After this, no modifications can be made to the order any more. However, if something is not working or if you have trouble finding the right page, you can contact our customer experience team <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a> to assist you.</p>",
"can-i-change-the-quantity-of-my-order-after-i-placed-it": "<p>Once you've placed your order, the quantity of items you've ordered is locked in. It's not possible to increase or decrease the quantity after checkout. However, if your order hasn't yet gone into production, you can cancel it and place a new order for the correct amount.</p><p>To check the status of the order you can follow these steps: </p><ol><li>Go to \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" in your account by hovering over your name in the top right of your screen.</li><li>Look at the 'status' section for the order you would like to edit.</li></ol><p>If your order has not gone into production yet, you can read <a href=\"help-article.html?q=can-i-cancel-my-order\">this article</a> on how to cancel your order. After that, you can place a new one with your preffered quatity.</p>",
"can-i-change-the-size-of-my-file-in-canva": "<p>At the moment, custom sizes are not yet available on Canva x HelloPrint.</p>",
"can-i-delete-my-account": "<p>Yes — but please note that deleting your account is permanent and can't be undone. Once your account is deleted you lose access to it for good: you won't be able to log back in, and your order history and saved details can't be recovered. If you'd like to use Helloprint again in future, you'll need to create a new account.</p><p>If you'd still like to go ahead, contact us via our <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact form</a> and select the 'Other' category, letting us know you'd like your account deleted.</p>",
"can-i-have-my-order-delivered-in-another-country": "<p>We can deliver orders in The Netherlands, Belgium, France, Ireland, Spain, Italy, Germany, Sweden, Ireland and the United Kingdom. In other countries, we do not deliver.</p><p>Delivery in of the countries above is only possible when the order is placed on that countries' website. You can find the list of countries where we deliver and their websites below:</p><p>United Kingdom: <a href=\"#home\">https://www.helloprint.com/en-gb/</a></p><p>The Netherlands: <a href=\"#nl-nl\">https://www.helloprint.com/nl-nl/</a></p><p>Ireland: <a href=\"#home\">https://www.helloprint.com/en-ie/</a></p><p>Belgium: <a href=\"#nl-be\">https://www.helloprint.com/nl-be/</a></p><p>France: <a href=\"#fr-fr\">https://www.helloprint.com/fr-fr/</a></p><p>Spain: <a href=\"#es-es\">https://www.helloprint.com/es-es/</a></p><p>Italy: <a href=\"#it-it\">https://www.helloprint.com/it-it/</a></p><p>Germany: <a href=\"#de-de\">https://www.helloprint.com/de-de/</a></p><p>Sweden: <a href=\"#sv-se\">https://www.helloprint.com/sv-se/</a></p>",
"can-i-have-my-order-delivered-to-a-fair-or-event": "<p>It is possible, but not recommended as it could cause delays, especially if there is no named recipient. We recommend that you provide a residential or business address to ensure prompt delivery.</p>",
"can-i-have-my-order-delivered-to-multiple-addresses": "<p>Did you know you can place a single order on HelloPrint and have it shipped to multiple locations? When checking out, simply add the destination addresses for each item in your cart. For instance, send a custom mug to your home office and a branded t-shirt to your brick-and-mortar store. Keep your order together but have it delivered wherever needed. No need to place separate orders for different locations.</p><p>You can do this by following these steps during checkout: </p><ol><li>While in your cart, go to 'Pay &amp; Upload Files.' This will first take you to the delivery options.</li><li>Choose the preferred address for each product. If your address isn't in your address book yet, you can add it by clicking 'Change Address' next to the house icon on the left side of your product details.</li><li>Once you have everything in place, proceed with the remainder of the checkout process.</li></ol><p><strong>Please note:</strong> It's not possible to split a single product across two addresses. For instance, if you want to send 1000 flyers to your home office and another 1000 to your store, please add them to your order as two separate products. This way, they will be packaged separately for delivery.</p>",
"can-i-have-products-packaged-separately-or-in-a-special-way": "<p>Although this isn't offered as a standard option in our ordering process, it can be requested. To determine whether it's possible for your order, and if any additional costs apply, please complete our <a href=\"#request-a-quote\">quote form</a>. We aim to respond with an offer within two business days.</p>",
"can-i-make-changes-to-my-file": "<p>If you haven't reviewed your digital proof yet but you already know you want to make changes to your current file, you can open the upload and proof page and select the following button: 'there is a mistake in my file/ I would like to upload a new file'. </p><p>This will lead you to a page where you can upload a new file. If you have already approved the digital proof, you will find a button to 'change the submitted file(s)'. Clicking this button will lead you to a page where you can re-upload your files. If this option is not shown, your order is probably already in production. </p><p>When your order is accepted or in production, changes are not possible anymore.</p>",
"can-i-pick-up-my-order": "<p>Unfortunately, this is not possible as an option since we work with many production locations across Europe.</p>",
"can-i-print-small-text-on-my-product": "<p>Thin lines and small text can be challenging to print clearly, especially if they are too close together or not bold enough. Therefore, it's important to check that these elements have the minimum size required for the given print technique and material so they will be legible in the final product.</p><p>On every product page, within the section 'Design Guidelines' we mention the minimum font size or line thickness in order for you to design it in a correct way.</p>",
"can-i-print-thin-lines-on-my-product": "<p>Thin lines and small text can be challenging to print clearly, especially if they are too close together or not bold enough. Therefore, it's important to check that these elements have the minimum size required for the given print technique and material so they will be legible in the final product.</p>",
"can-i-repeat-a-previous-order": "<p>Yes, you can easily repeat a previous order.</p><p>In order to do so, follow the following steps:</p><ol><li> Go to '<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>' in your account by hovering over your name in the top right of your screen.</li><li>Go to the order overview page of the specific order you would like to repeat by clicking on 'order details', which you can find right next to your order information. </li><li><p>Once you have landed on the order detail page, you can click on the 'reorder’ button under the product you want to reorder. </p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-977e003894/e697635e72c2bc13da87864c5618757e/977e003894-screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2012-58-16-tgk.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2012-58-16-tgk.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li><p>Select the products you would like to reorder and click on 'add products to cart'. If your previous order has an artwork and you want to reorder it using the same artwork, select ‘With this design’. </p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-628f4697da/06a8c17da9514987d392988499d6455a/628f4697da-screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2013-00-07-ojs.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2013-00-07-ojs.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li><p>If you need to make any changes to the product specifications, no problem! Click on the pencil icon, and you'll be taken to the product page where you can adjust the specifications. If everything looks good, you can simply proceed to \"Pay &amp; Upload\". Here, you can choose your preferred payment method and upload your files if you are reordering without artwork. </p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-c7fc687a2a/f07a80415b8004c498c4aebb0a9f02df/c7fc687a2a-screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2013-03-40-atw.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-06-20at-2013-03-40-atw.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li> If you tried to repeat your order, but our website ends up giving you an error message, we probably changed something in our backend for that specific product which prevents us to offer the repeat. As a customer, you can order the same product by going to the product page on our website and selecting the same specifications and quantities as before. If that does not work, you can contact us via our <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact form</a>.</li></ol>",
"can-i-request-a-sample": "<p>If you would like to receive a sample, it is best to order the minimum quantity of the product you require - you can find this information on the individual product pages after filling in your desired specifications.</p><p><strong>Please note:</strong> A small print run may be produced differently to a larger print run due to the printing methods - the colours may differ, but the materials, however, are the same.</p>",
"can-i-return-my-order": "<h2>Personalised products</h2><p>First things first, what is a personalised product? A personalised product is any item that is printed, engraved or otherwise customised with your design or specifications. Because these products are made to order:</p><ul><li>They cannot be returned</li><li>There is no cooling-off period</li></ul><p>This is because customised products are created specifically for you and cannot be resold. Of course, if your order arrives damaged or there is a production issue, please contact us. We’ll always review the situation and help you find a solution.</p><h2>Non-personalised products</h2><p>Some products in our assortment are not personalised (for example, blank or unprinted items). For these products, a standard 14-day cooling-off period applies. This means:</p><ul><li>You have 14 calendar days from the day you receive your order to request a return</li><li>The product must be unused</li><li>The product must be returned in its original, undamaged packaging</li><li>Return shipping costs are borne by the customer</li></ul><p>To request a return, please contact our customer service team within 14 days of receiving your order. We’ll provide you with the return instructions and address.</p><h2>Not sure what applies to your order?</h2><p>If you’re unsure whether your product is personalised or eligible for return, feel free to contact us. We’re happy to help.</p>",
"can-i-see-a-proof-before-paying-for-my-order": "<ol><li> Add your product(s) to your cart.</li><li>Once you have added all products to the cart, select \"Continue\".</li><li>Choose your delivery options and continue to payment.</li><li>Select \"Pay later and upload my artwork first\" on the payment page to upload your artwork and see a proof before paying for the order.</li><li>Upload your artwork, and we will show you a proof to approve. If you are unhappy with the proof, you can opt to upload a new file or contact us.</li><li>Don't forget to pay your order, otherwise your order will not go in production.</li></ol>",
"can-i-speed-up-my-order-that-is-already-in-production": "<p>If you ordered a specific product on a certain turnaround time and your order is in production, we can unfortunately not speed-up the production or delivery time. </p><p>We work with more than 300 suppliers, who all have their own deadlines and production times. If an order is taken into production, the turnaround time is set and planning has been made. We cannot offer any speed-up after this, not even with extra payment.</p>",
"can-i-use-a-po-box-as-a-delivery-address": "<p>Unfortunately, this isn’t an option. Please always provide a residential or business address.</p><p><strong>Please note:</strong> Have you opted for Saturday delivery? Then do not provide a business address. To ensure that your delivery actually takes place on Saturday, we need a consumer address.\"</p>",
"can-i-use-borders-or-frames-in-my-design": "<p>We advise against this, as there’s a chance that the frame will not be in proportion on all sides after the trimming process, and your design may look off-centre. The borders in your artwork will make even just a few mm’s difference in the cut very noticeable. This is not something we can avoid.</p>",
"can-my-order-be-delivered-urgently": "<p>We offer next-day delivery for a wide range of our products. You can check the availability and cost of delivery for each product by visiting its individual product page.</p>",
"can-we-create-a-design-for-you": "<p>We can not make your files from scratch, however we are happy to make some small changes for you. Interested? <a href=\"#new2contactform\">Let us know</a> what exactly you want to change and we will let you know if it is possible!</p>",
"can-you-deliver-to-other-countries": "<p>This site serves the Republic of Ireland, with delivery in euro (€).</p><p>In Northern Ireland? Please use our UK site instead — it delivers in pounds (€) with IE VAT. You can switch at any time using the country selector at the top of the page.</p><p>Want your order delivered in another country? Place it on that country's Helloprint site, and we'll deliver locally there.</p>",
"company-account-how-it-works": "<h3>What is a company account?</h3><p>With a company account, you can invite your colleagues to collaborate on ordering at HelloPrint. With a company account, you and your colleagues can place orders, approve artwork, and share invoices. </p><ul><li>Want to give your designer access to upload and approve designs for your orders?</li><li>Need to share invoices for your orders with your colleagues from accounting?</li><li>Going on leave and planning to hand over your orders to a colleague?</li></ul><p>Access our “Company Account” feature from the “My Account” page. Invite your colleagues and start the collaboration.</p><h3></h3><h3>Create a company account </h3><p>To create a “Company Account\" log in to HelloPrint with your email, go to “Create Company Account” in “My Account” Add your company name to set up the account. You can also include your VAT number and Chamber of Commerce information. Your personal information including the first name, last name and email will be filled in automatically after you create the account.</p><p>As the account creator, you will be the first user of your company account and the contact person. Once the account is created you will gain access to the “Manage Users” page where you can invite other colleagues.</p><h3>Users overview</h3><p>You can see all users in your company account on the “Manage users” page in “My Account”. In the overview, you will see all the users with their status. You can also invite new users and remove users on this page. </p><p>If the user is invited but has not yet accepted or rejected the invite, their status will be “Invited”.</p><p>If the user has accepted the invitation and joined the company account, their status will be “Active”.</p><p>If the user has rejected the invitation, their status will be “Rejected”. In case you want to re-invite a user who previously rejected the invitation, you can delete the user on the “Manage users” page and invite them again.</p><h3>Inviting new users</h3><p>To start collaborating, invite new users to join your company account. To do so, go to the “Manage users” page in “My account”. </p><p>To invite a user, you need to provide their email address, alongside their first and last name. You can invite multiple users simultaneously to the company account. Invited users will receive an invitation via email. The invitation expires after 96 hours, after which you can send the user a new invitation if needed. Once the invitation is successfully sent, you will receive a confirmation email from us. </p><p>Once a new user is invited, they receive an email with the invitation which they can accept or reject. If they accept the invitation, the user will be redirected to the “Company Account” page on “My Account”. If the user does not have a HelloPrint account yet, they will need to create one before accepting the invitation. If the user rejects the invitation, you can delete their record in the “Manage Users” page and re-invite them if needed.</p><p>You will be updated on the status of your invitations via email and on the “Manage Users” page.</p><p>Once a new user joins your company account, they will be able to see all the orders placed by the company account members, access the shared address book and the invoices. They will also get permission to add users to the company account, set a contact person, and edit or delete the company account.</p><h3>User permissions in a company account</h3><p>All the users in a company account can view all the orders placed by the company account members in their HelloPrint account. They can access the shared address book and invoices. They are also allowed to add new users to the company account, set a contact person and edit or delete the company account.</p><h3>Orders, invoices and addresses of the company account</h3><p>To view the orders, you can go to the “Orders” page. As a company account member, you will view all the orders your active colleagues placed by their HelloPrint account.</p><p>To view the invoices, you can go to the “Invoices” page. Here you will have access to all the invoices of orders placed by your colleagues with their HelloPrint account.</p><p>To view the addresses, you can go to the “Addresses” page. As a company account member, you will view all the addresses saved by your colleagues in their HelloPrint account.</p><h3>Deleting users</h3><p>If you would like to remove any users from the company account, you can do so on the “Manage users” page in “My Account”. Click on the “Delete” icon next to the user you want to delete. </p><p>If a user is deleted, they will lose access to the company account details and the orders placed by colleagues. Users will keep their Helloprint account and all the orders placed by them (including the orders they placed as part of the company account). </p><p>After a user is deleted, The orders they placed before joining the company account will no longer exist in the company account. This can affect the VIP level of the company account as the order history of these users will no longer count towards the annual print spend of the company account.</p><h3></h3><h3>Leaving the company account</h3><p>If you would like to leave the company account you can go to the “Manage Users” page in “My Account”. After you leave the company account, you will lose access to all shared invoices, orders and addresses. You will keep access to all the orders you placed with your HelloPrint account (also placed while part of the company account) and your VIP level will be recalculated based on your own orders.</p><h3>VIP logic for company accounts</h3><p>Company accounts follow the same VIP logic as all other accounts. All users of the company account share the same VIP level as the company account and enjoy the relevant discounts and benefits.</p><p>The annual print spend for the company account is calculated based on the sum of the annual print spends of all current users. Orders placed before users were invited to company accounts are also included in the calculation of the VIP level.</p><p>If a new user is added to the organisation, their annual print spend is included in the calculation of the VIP level. </p><p>If a user is deleted, the orders they placed while being part of the company account still count towards the annual print spend. The orders placed before users were invited to company accounts will not be included anymore.</p><h3>Setting a contact person </h3><p>The contact person of the company is the person we will contact in case we need to send any specific company-related information.</p><p>All users can change the contact person by selecting a different active user in the “Manage users” page of the company account.</p><p>By default, the person who starts the company account is the contact person. If there is only one user in the organisation, they will be considered the contact person for the company account.</p><h3>Editing the company account details</h3><p>If you want to edit your company account details you can do so on the “Company details” page. On this page, you can change the company name, your VAT number and Chamber of Commerce information. All active members of the company account can edit these details.</p><h3>Deleting company account</h3><p>You can delete the company account via the page “Company details”. To delete the account, click “Delete” and confirm.</p><p>All users of the company account have the permission to delete it.</p><p>If the account is deleted, all users will lose access to shared addresses, invoices, and orders. Each user will have the orders they placed with their HelloPrint account and each VIP level will be defined on individual annual print spend.</p>",
"creating-a-company-account": "<p>To create a company account, go to “Create company account” in My Account. Add your company name to set up the account. You can also add your VAT number and Chamber of Commerce information. </p><p>You will be the first user of your company account and you can invite more users once the account is created.</p>",
"do-i-need-to-add-trim-marks-to-my-design": "<p>Registration marks ensure that all the colours in the printed artwork are correctly aligned, which is why these marks are printed using 100% of each ink in the CMYK mix. It's important to avoid using this colour as a design element since it could result in text blurriness or smudges on the final product.</p><p>It is not necessary for you to add trim marks, we will always add them during our check.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-2330be17ca/6b9cab0cbfc1e5a158663bba249e989a/2330be17ca-screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-25-27-rhe.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-25-27-rhe.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"do-i-need-to-embed-the-images-in-my-design": "<p> Embedding includes all necessary information about an image within the artwork file to be properly reproduced during printing.</p>",
"do-i-need-to-have-an-account-to-place-an-order": "<p>Yes, you do need an <a href=\"#login\">account</a> before you can place an order.</p>",
"do-i-need-to-pay-vat": "<p>VAT is included where it applies, and the exact amount is always shown itemised in your basket and on your invoice.</p><p>Whether VAT applies — and how much — can depend on the product and how it's used, so it's calculated for your specific order at checkout rather than quoted as a single rate. You'll always see the VAT before you complete your order.</p>",
"does-my-order-go-directly-in-production-when-i-select-the-pay-by-invoice": "<p>Once you've chosen the \"pay on invoice\" option while placing your order, your order will swiftly move into production once your artwork is approved. Following the successful delivery of your order, we will promptly send you an invoice. Upon receiving the invoice, your payment term will commence.</p><p>This is different than when you would choose 'pay by bank transfer' where your order will go into production once we've received your payment.</p>",
"give-us-a-call": "<p>Sometimes you just want to speak to someone directly. Our team of print experts is happy to help you over the phone.</p><p><strong>Call us at:</strong> (+44) 121 285 7464<strong>Opening hours:</strong> Monday to Friday, 09h00–17h00 (GMT+1)</p><p>For faster support, we still recommend using our <strong>24/7 chat</strong> at the bottom right of the website but if you prefer a call, we’ll be glad to assist you.</p>",
"how-can-i-change-my-invoice-address": "<p>If you would like to change the billing address for an order which does not have an invoice yet, you can change the billing address on the order detail page in <a href=\"#my-account\">My Account</a>.</p><p>If the invoice has already been created for your order or you do not see an option to change your billing address on the order detail page, fill out our <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact form</a> with your invoice number and your new address, and we will gladly make the necessary changes for you!</p>",
"how-can-i-change-my-password": "<p>To change your password, ensure that you are logged in and simply click on <a href=\"#my-account\">this link</a>. Once you are there, navigate to the 'Change your details' section, where you can update your password.</p>",
"how-can-i-change-the-design-i-made-in-canva-once-i-accept-it": "<p>You can change the design as long as your order hasn’t been paid for. To do this simply go back to the design to make changes. If your order has already been paid for, just <a href=\"#new2contactform\">get in touch</a> with our printexperts team we can do our best to help!</p>",
"how-can-i-change-the-email-address-where-i-receive-my-invoices": "<p>At HelloPrint, you can easily update your account information, such as your invoice email address, by following these steps: </p><ol><li> Go to '<a href=\"#my-account\">My Account</a>' by hovering over your name in the top right corner of your screen.</li><li>Scroll down until you see the field 'Change Your Details.'</li><li>Fill out your preferred email address in the 'Invoice Email' section.</li><li>Click 'Save.'</li></ol>",
"how-can-i-create-an-account": "<p>You can create an account by filling in the fields <a href=\"#login\">here</a> with your information.</p>",
"how-can-i-download-designs-from-my-previous-orders": "<p>You can download your previous designs in \"My account\".</p><ol><li>Go to \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" in \"<a href=\"#my-account\">My account</a>\"</li><li>Select the order from which you want to download the designs</li><li>On the order page, you can download the original artwork you uploaded and a print-ready PDF we use for the print.</li></ol><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-22dec7f176/c24fd83d23645c6556f507c76e9f6ef7/22dec7f176-screenshot2024-10-14at165625-tla.png\" alt=\"screenshot2024-10-14at165625-tla.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"how-can-i-find-my-previous-canva-designs": "<p>We offer Canva as a third-party design tool on our platform, but please note that we do not have access to Canva's premium features. This means you won't be able to download Canva files directly or save designs for extended periods on our platform.</p><p>To view your saved Canva designs, go to the <strong>\"Design Online\"</strong> section, where you'll find a <strong>\"My Designs\"</strong> tab. Any designs saved during your session will be stored here.</p><p>Please be aware that because we provide a <strong>design-straight-to-production service</strong>, your designs may disappear if you close the design program before moving forward with production or if the files have already been processed for production.</p><p>If you're unable to locate a Canva design you’ve previously worked on but have already placed an order using that design, you can retrieve it by providing your order number to our customer service team. They will help recover the design from your past order.</p>",
"how-can-i-find-the-right-size-in-canva": "<p>If you click ‘File’ on the upper left corner of the editor, you can see the dimensions of the file.</p>",
"how-can-i-join-the-non-profit-program": "<p>You can join by filling in the form on <a>this</a> page. Once submitted, our team will verify your organisation and notify you of the outcome by email. Upon approval, you will be entitled to exclusive discounts on all future orders!</p>",
"how-can-i-track-my-order": "<p>Once your order has been shipped, you will receive a confirmation email with tracking information.</p><p>You can also view the status of your shipment by logging into <a href=\"#my-account\">Your Account</a>, selecting the 'orders' tab on the left side of the page, and select the order of which you want to view the status. This way, you can easily stay informed about the progress of your order.</p>",
"how-come-elements-in-my-design-have-moved-after-downloading-it-from-canva": "<p>Different browsers can export some elements differently. If elements in your design appear to have moved or changed size during download, try to download your design again on a different browser. The best browsers for Canva are Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari and Microsoft Edge.</p>",
"how-do-i-add-a-discount-voucher-to-my-order": "<p>Add your discount voucher by following the steps below:</p><ol><li>Go to <a href=\"#cart\">the cart</a> to finalise the purchase</li><li>Click the tab 'Do you have a discount code?' beneath the 'Continue'-button.</li><li>A box will appear where you can enter your voucher code</li><li>Click 'Save' to add the voucher to your order</li><li>The website will recalculate the total amount and show the discounted amount</li><li>Click 'Continue' to proceed with the order at the discounted price</li></ol><p><strong>Please note:</strong> after payment and completing an order, you can no longer add a discount code.</p>",
"how-do-i-add-an-extra-page-to-my-design-when-using-canva-i-e-for-double-sided-pr": "<p>You can click ‘+ page’ below the template. You can then scroll between pages.</p>",
"how-do-i-add-elements-borders-etc-when-using-canva": "<p>Click the elements tab from the side panel and use the search bar to look for specific elements. You can also browse all elements by clicking “See all”. Elements include shapes, lines, illustrations, icons, frames, grids, stickers, charts and gradients. If you want to add a border, simply follow the same process but search ‘borders’ in the search bar.</p>",
"how-do-i-add-exclusive-finishes-to-my-design-for-products-with-spot-uv-or-exclus": "<p>To ensure that the exclusive finishes are applied correctly, you need to provide two files: </p><ul><li>One with your complete design (single or double-sided).</li><li>Another with only the elements of your design where the finish should be applied.</li></ul><p>In the second file, make sure to indicate with 100% black where the exclusive finish should be applied. Keep in mind that the exclusive finish cannot be applied fully to the edge. For more information and templates, please refer to the product page of the desired product. There you will find a guide on how to correctly set up your files.</p>",
"how-do-i-approve-my-proof": "<p>When your proof is ready you'll get an email, and the order shows <strong>Action needed</strong> in your account under <strong>Orders</strong>.</p><ol><li>Open the order and choose <strong>Approve proof</strong>.</li><li>Check the proof carefully — front and back. Use the <strong>Trim</strong> and <strong>Bleed</strong> overlays to see exactly where the paper is cut, and zoom in on text and logos.</li><li>Read the pre-flight notes beside the proof: anything we fixed automatically or want you to double-check is listed there. (<a href=\"help-article.html?q=what-are-the-pre-flight-notes-on-my-proof\">Understanding pre-flight notes</a>)</li><li><p>Choose one of three actions:</p><ul><li><strong>Approve &amp; send to production</strong> — printing starts immediately and the file can no longer be changed.</li><li><strong>Upload new artwork</strong> — replaces your file and generates a fresh proof (this can shift your delivery date).</li><li><strong>Chat about this artwork</strong> — unsure about anything? Ask us first.</li></ul></li></ol><p>Mind the <strong>approval deadline</strong> shown beside the proof — approve in time to keep your delivery date. (<a href=\"help-article.html?q=what-happens-if-i-miss-my-proof-approval-deadline\">What if I miss it?</a>)</p>",
"how-do-i-attach-files-to-my-message": "<p>Photos or documents often say more than words — you can attach them when you send your message. Look for the Attach files field on the form.</p><p>What we can accept:</p><ul><li>Photos: JPEG, PNG or HEIC</li><li>Documents: PDF, DOCX or TXT</li><li>Up to 5 files per message, 10 MB each</li></ul><p>For print-quality problems, a clear photo of the printed product in daylight helps us resolve things fastest.</p>",
"how-do-i-cancel-a-specific-product-instead-of-my-entire-order": "<p>To cancel a specific item from your order, follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Go to the '<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>' page in 'My Account'.</li><li><p>Locate the relevant order and click on the 'Order Information' button.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-0346f2ac80/aaf37e4d9ae985dc87064c3b16a44477/0346f2ac80-1701776433198-kue.png\" alt=\"1701776433198-kue.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li><p>Click on the button labeled 'Cancel Item' at the bottom of the product you wish to cancel.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-e8818f0e4d/0f74b03c9bb005b46e8bb2b07132b88e/e8818f0e4d-screenshot-202023-12-05-20at-2014-07-47-mju.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-12-05-20at-2014-07-47-mju.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li>Select the product(s) you want to cancel.</li><li><p>Click 'Continue' </p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-f13a4b10c5/4e01138fd734e689e061e16b8e317cd6/f13a4b10c5-screenshot-202023-12-05-20at-2014-08-21-vnw.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-12-05-20at-2014-08-21-vnw.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></li><li>Choose a cancellation reason from the menu.</li><li>Click on 'Yes, cancel my order'.</li><li>That's it! By following these steps, you have successfully canceled a product in your order.</li></ol><p><em>To ensure that everything has been processed correctly, you will receive a confirmation email from us. You can also keep an eye on the '</em><a href=\"#orders\"><em>Orders</em></a><em>' page to see if the status of your order has been successfully changed to 'Cancelled'.</em></p>",
"how-do-i-change-my-artwork-file-after-uploading": "<p>You can change your artwork files as long as your order is not in production yet. You can check the status of your order per product in your order overview. If your order is already in production, we cannot make any further changes to your files.</p><p>To change the artwork files and view the status of your order do the following:</p><ol><li>Go to \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" in your account by hovering your name on the top right of your screen</li><li>Click on \"Order details\" for the order you would like to edit</li><li>Click on \"Change submitted files'' to change your artwork</li></ol>",
"how-do-i-change-my-delivery-address-after-ordering": "<ol><li>Open the order under <strong>My Account → Orders</strong>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Change shipping address</strong> in the Self-service panel.</li><li>Pick a saved address or enter a new one (include the <strong>Eircode</strong>), and save.</li></ol><p>Two rules to know:</p><ul><li>The new address must be in the <strong>same country</strong> as your order — each HelloPrint site delivers within its own country.</li><li>Once a parcel's delivery label is printed, the address is locked. If that happens while you're editing you'll see a message — <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and we'll check what the carrier can still do.</li></ul>",
"how-do-i-download-my-invoices-and-credit-notes": "<p>Every invoice and credit note is in <strong>My Account → Invoices</strong> as a PDF — and we email the invoice when your order ships.</p><ol><li>Open <strong>My Account → Invoices</strong>.</li><li>Find the order — search by order number or date.</li><li>Download the invoice or credit note PDF.</li></ol>",
"how-do-i-file-a-complaint": "<p>If something isn't right with your order, you can let us know in a couple of minutes.</p><p>Open the order in My Account and select “Report a problem”, or go to My Account → Support and start a new message, choosing the category that fits.</p><p>Tell us what went wrong and we'll investigate. Where the fault is ours, we'll put it right — usually a reprint, refund or credit. You can follow your message, its status and our reply under My Account → Support; each one has its own reference (for example C-A3F9C2D1).</p>",
"how-do-i-get-a-quote-for-a-bespoke-product": "<p><a href=\"#request-a-quote\">Request a quote</a> for it: tell us the specs you have — dimensions, material, quantity, deadline — and our team sources it through our production network and comes back with a price.</p><p>The more specifics you give (a reference photo helps enormously), the faster and sharper the quote.</p>",
"how-do-i-increase-my-credit-limit": "<p>If you're looking to extend your purchasing power with HelloPrint, increasing your credit limit is an easy process. Here's how it works:</p><ol><li><strong>Contact Our Team:</strong> Contact our Customer Experience <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a>. They'll guide you through the necessary steps and ensure you have the information needed, like your Chamber of Commerce number.</li><li><strong>Credit Check:</strong> We'll do a quick credit assessment to better understand your current financial situation. Don't worry, it's confidential. This helps us determine an appropriate new credit limit for you.</li><li><strong>Decision &amp; Notification:</strong> Our team reviews the information and decides on your new limit. We'll let you know the outcome right away through your preferred method of contact.</li></ol>",
"how-do-i-manage-my-addresses": "<p>Your address book lives in <strong>My Account → Addresses</strong>: add, edit or delete addresses and set your default shipping address. Include the <strong>Eircode</strong> on every address.</p><p>One distinction worth knowing: the address book sets where <em>future</em> orders go. To change where an <strong>existing order</strong> is delivered, do it from the order page — (<a href=\"help-article.html?q=how-do-i-change-my-delivery-address-after-ordering\">here's how</a>).</p>",
"how-do-i-order-a-custom-size": "<p>Selected products — currently <strong>stickers</strong> and <strong>panels</strong> — accept custom dimensions: choose <strong>Custom size</strong> in the configurator, enter width and height in mm, and the price updates instantly.</p><p>Don't see it on the product you want? Look for the <strong>Custom size</strong> option in the configurator — we're adding it to more products over time.</p>",
"how-do-i-order-printed-products-with-multiple-designs": "<p>If you would like to print multiple designs of the same product, we offer this option for multiple products on our website, like banners, panels and custom-size flags.</p><p>To do this, select the total quantity you want to order, then select the total number of unique designs and specify the quantity per design. Keep in mind, that it is only possible to order up to 30 different designs online. If you would like to order more than 30 designs, you can contact <a href=\"#request-a-quote\">our Bespoke team</a>.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-17305e8ed8/515e09ab00c4257f3dae1b1e62e3d04b/17305e8ed8-screenshot2024-04-29at140446-hd0.png\" alt=\"screenshot2024-04-29at140446-hd0.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Once the order is placed, you can upload your designs separately for each variant. We aim to produce and ship all your designs at the same time, therefore, once you upload some of your designs, we will wait until all your designs are uploaded and approved before producing your order.</p><p>If the product you want to order does not have an option to select a number of designs online, you can follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Add each product separately to your shopping cart.</li><li>Upload the corresponding design file for each product.</li></ol><p>For example, if you want to purchase four A3 posters, each with a distinct design, add four individual posters to your cart and upload a unique design file for each.</p>",
"how-do-i-pay-on-invoice": "<p>We offer all customers an option to pay on invoice. To be eligible, you must have placed and completed at least three orders with us.</p><p><strong>Payment terms</strong></p><p>Once this option is available, you can place an order and pay for it within 14 days of receiving the invoice. This is our standard payment term.</p><p><strong>Credit limit</strong></p><p>Our standard credit limit is €250. If you reach this limit, the option to pay by invoice will be temporarily disabled until outstanding invoices are paid.</p><p><strong>Requesting different payment terms or credit limit</strong></p><p>If you need a higher credit limit, or different payment terms, or want to enable the invoice payment option earlier, please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact our support team</a>. We review requests on a case-by-case basis and will inform you if we can accommodate your needs.</p>",
"how-do-i-request-a-quote": "<p>Need a quantity, size or finish the product page doesn't offer — or a formal quote for sign-off? <a href=\"#request-a-quote\">Request a quote</a> and tell us what you need, and we'll <strong>email your quote back</strong> with prices and delivery options.</p><p>Not sure what you need? Our print experts can help you spec it — just say so in your request and we'll talk it through.</p>",
"how-do-i-reset-my-password": "<p>Can't get into your account? Here's how to get back in:</p><ol><li>Choose <strong>Forgotten password?</strong> on the login page — the reset link arrives by email within minutes (check your spam folder too).</li><li>No email coming through? You may have registered with a different address — try the one on your order confirmation.</li><li>Still locked out? Check you're on the right country shop — your account is linked to the country site you registered on.</li></ol><p>None of that worked? <a href=\"#new2contactform\">Chat with us</a> and we'll recover access together.</p><p>Want to change your password while you're logged in? Go to <strong>My Account → Details → Change password</strong>.</p>",
"how-do-i-track-a-multi-parcel-order": "<p>Orders with several products often ship in several parcels — sometimes from different production partners, on different days. That's normal, and each parcel is tracked separately.</p><p>On your order page every parcel has its own card: the carrier, the tracking link, the expected date, and <strong>which items are inside</strong>. One parcel arriving doesn't mean the rest aren't coming — check each card.</p><p>All parcels show \"delivered\" but something's missing? <a href=\"#new2contactform\">Report a problem</a> and we'll sort it.</p>",
"how-do-i-unsubscribe-from-the-newsletter": "<p>It's completely understandable if you wish to unsubscribe from our newsletter. This article is designed to guide you through the process. Here's a simple step-by-step guide to help you unsubscribe:</p><ol><li>Visit '<a href=\"#my-account\">My Account</a>' by hovering your cursor over your name in the top right corner of your screen.</li><li>Click on 'Email preferences' located in the My Account options on the left side of the screen.</li><li>Select or deselect the types of emails you wish to receive from us.</li><li>Click the blue 'update email preferences' button to confirm your selections.</li></ol><p>If you've unchecked all topics but still receive emails from us, please don't hesitate to reach out to our print experts <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a>. We'll investigate the issue and ensure it's resolve.</p>",
"how-do-i-update-my-company-and-vat-details": "<p>Your company name and VAT number live in <strong>My Account → Personal Details</strong>, in the <strong>Company info</strong> card. Edit them there, and your VAT number appears on every invoice from the moment you save it.</p><p>Need a different company name, VAT number or registration on a specific shipping address — for example a subsidiary? Set those per address in <strong>My Account → Addresses</strong> when you add or edit the address.</p>",
"how-do-i-upload-and-preview-my-file-in-the-editor": "<p>On supported products you can upload your file straight into the online editor and see it placed on the product <em>before</em> adding to basket. That preview follows your item into the basket and checkout, so you always know which design belongs to which item.</p><p>Good to know: this basket preview is a quick visual check. After you order and we run our pre-flight check, two files become available: your <strong>print proof</strong> — a clean preview of how it prints, without trim lines or print marks — and the <strong>production PDF</strong>, which does include the print marks. (<a href=\"help-article.html?q=how-do-i-approve-my-proof\">How do I approve my proof?</a>)</p>",
"how-do-i-upload-my-multi-page-or-double-sided-artwork": "<p>For example, when designing a 6-page stapled booklet, arrange pages front to back, 1 to 6. For a double-sided product like a business card, just submit one artwork with two pages - one for the front and one for the back. Our printing process will automatically detect page/side placements to achieve your intended final layout.</p><p>Keeping your entire design in one file streamlines the uploading and ordering process, and ensures cohesion across all pages. Your one print-ready file is all we need to bring your creative vision to life.</p><p>If you want to order the same product, but with different designs, please read <a href=\"help-article.html?q=how-do-i-order-printed-products-with-multiple-designs\">this article.</a></p>",
"how-do-i-upload-my-own-images-in-canva": "<p>You can upload your own images to use in your designs. From the editor side panel, click the tab “uploads”. Select and drag the image to upload it or click the “upload” button. Once it’s been uploaded, you can click on the image to add it to your design. You can then easily resize your images, adjust their settings or apply special filters and effects within Canva! Still unsure? </p><p>Check out Canva’s tutorials <a href=\"#design-create-and-print-like-a-pro-with-canva-and-helloprint\">here</a>, or <a href=\"#new2contactform\">get in touch</a> with our customer experience team who would be happy to help!</p>",
"how-do-refunds-work": "<p>Refunds always go back to your original payment method, automatically.</p><ul><li><strong>After a cancellation</strong> — once your cancellation is confirmed you receive a credit note and the refund is triggered. Allow 3–8 working days depending on your bank.</li><li><strong>Overpaid?</strong> We detect it and refund the difference without you asking.</li><li><strong>After an issue</strong> — once your issue is resolved and a refund agreed, allow 3–8 working days for it to reach your account, depending on your bank.</li></ul><p>Refund not arrived after 8 working days? <a href=\"#new2contactform\">Contact us</a> with your order number and we'll trace it with the payment provider.</p>",
"how-does-the-lowest-price-guarantee-work": "<p>We can offer you the lowest price guarantee if you compare the exact same product. That means we look at the print run, size, exact same product specifications and delivery time. Send us a message <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a> with a link to the product you're comparing. We'll let you know if we can match the lowest price. </p><p>This does not apply to orders that you already paid and placed in production with us.</p>",
"how-long-does-a-reply-usually-take": "<p>Most messages get a first reply within 2 business hours. During busy periods it can take a little longer — we always reply in the order messages come in.</p><p>You don't need to wait around — we'll send you an email as soon as we reply.</p>",
"how-long-does-an-artwork-check-take": "<p>The expert review time depends on current order deadlines, but we always deliver proofs before your deadline. If your order is paid or ordered by invoice/Sprinque, you will receive your proof within 24h. Please note that the majority of our artwork experts are covering the checks during standard business hours. </p><p>No matter if your artwork has been checked automatic or manual, HelloPrint always aims to provide helpful, technical advice so you feel empowered to design and print with confidence.</p>",
"how-much-ink-coverage-should-i-use-for-the-best-end-result": "<p>Ink coverage refers to the percentage of ink used on a printed product. The more ink used, the higher the coverage, which can affect the final appearance of the printed piece. For example, too much ink can cause smudging, bleeding, or even damage to the paper. This is why we recommend using a maximum ink coverage of 300% for most of our products.</p>",
"how-to-get-in-touch": "<p>Need help? We’re here for you!</p><p><strong>Chat with us (fastest!)</strong>Our team is available 24/7, via the chat button at the bottom right of the website. Most questions are solved instantly.</p><p><strong>Email us</strong>Please send us an email to <a href=\"mailto:hello@helloprint.com\">hello@helloprint.com</a>. We’ll get back to you within <strong>48 hours (Monday–Friday)</strong>. Please note that emails sent over the weekend will be handled from Monday onwards.</p>",
"i-can-not-log-in-what-should-i-do": "<p>If you're having trouble logging in, we’re here to help! Please follow these steps:</p><p>Make sure you are on the Helloprint website for your region. If your account is registered with a different Helloprint site, you won’t be able to log in from this one.</p><p>Try resetting your password by clicking the “Forgot my password” button on the login page.</p>",
"i-can-t-find-the-product-i-m-looking-for-what-can-i-do": "<p>You can reach out to us via chat or fill in <a href=\"#request-a-quote\">a quote form</a>, so our print experts can help you out with a bespoke order. We'll get back to you with a competitive offer as soon as possible.</p>",
"i-don-t-see-all-my-designs-on-the-print-proof": "<p>It looks like you've uploaded multiple designs to a single order or order line. Unfortunately, this will cause issues such as the files being declined or only one design being visible. Our system allows only one design per order item or print run as mentioned on most product pages. </p><p><strong>How to Resolve:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>If you have multiple order lines</strong> but uploaded all designs to one order item, please divide the designs across the correct order lines.</li><li><strong>If you need more order lines</strong>, the order needs to be upgraded to so we can print all designs.</li></ol><p>You can resolve this by canceling the current order and creating a new one with the correct setup.</p>",
"i-have-a-very-big-file-how-can-i-upload-this": "<p>We understand that sometimes your creativity knows no bounds, and your artwork files can be quite extensive. Don't worry; we've got you covered! If you have a very big file to upload, follow this simple guide to ensure a smooth and hassle-free experience.</p><p><strong>Step 1: Automatic Notification</strong></p><p>When you attempt to upload your artwork, our system is designed to be intuitive and helpful. If your file is too large for our standard upload process, you'll receive an automatic notification. This notification will inform you that your file size exceeds the limit and provide you with an alternative solution.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Alternative Upload Form</strong></p><p>Click on the provided link to access our alternative upload form. This form is specifically designed to accommodate larger files, ensuring that you can still submit your artwork conveniently. Rest assured, we've streamlined this process to make it as user-friendly as possible.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Still Experiencing Issues?</strong></p><p>In the rare event that your file remains too large for the alternative upload form, we've got one more solution up our sleeves! You can easily send your files via WeTransfer, a trusted file-sharing service. Here's how:</p><ul><li>Visit WeTransfer on your browser.</li><li>Click \"Add your files\" and select the large artwork file(s) you want to send.</li><li>Enter \"<a href=\"mailto:hello@helloprint.ie\">hello@helloprint.ie</a>\" as the recipient's email address.</li><li>Enter your own email address, so we can confirm receipt and link the files to your order.</li><li>Include your order number in the message form.</li><li>Click \"Transfer\" to start the upload.</li><li>WeTransfer will generate a download link, which you can include in your email or order notes for reference.</li></ul><p>If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don't hesitate to reach out to our friendly support team. We're here to help you every step of the way. Happy designing!</p>",
"i-have-cancelled-my-order-why-have-i-not-received-my-refund": "<p>It's likely that the payment has been linked to another order that was created to replace the cancelled one If that's not the case, please check your open invoices in <a href=\"#my-account\">Your Account</a>, as it's possible that the refund has not been processed yet due to outstanding payments.</p><p>Please note that the amount will be transferred using the payment method you initially used. This usually takes 3-8 working days to process.</p><p>If neither of these reasons apply, please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> so we can investigate the issue further.</p>",
"i-have-not-received-my-invoice-now-what": "<p>If you have not received your invoice via email yet, check the invoices in <a href=\"#my-account\">your account</a>.</p><p>If you can't see the correct invoice or you want to receive it earlier, you can <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> so we can send it to you.</p>",
"i-have-overpaid-my-order-how-can-this-be-resolved": "<p>When you pay twice for the same order, our system detects the excess and refunds it automatically. This can take up to 5 working days. If it hasn't arrived by then, <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and we'll help.</p>",
"i-m-missing-the-accessory-i-ordered-with-my-purchase-what-now": "<ol><li> Sometimes, accessories are shipped separately. Have you received multiple tracking codes?</li><li>Check with your neighbors and search carefully for any secure hiding spots where the delivery carrier might have placed your order.</li><li>If you've thoroughly looked around and still can't locate your package, please reach out to us via <a href=\"#new2contactform\">this form</a>. We are committed to resolving this for you. When you contact us, select the 'Complaint' and clearly mention the order, delivered items, and what's missing. Also attach photos of the products you did receive, the box, and the label. These images will greatly assist us in expediting the resolution process.</li></ol>",
"is-it-important-to-outline-my-text": "<p>Embedding includes all necessary information about a font or image within the artwork file to be adequately reproduced during printing.</p>",
"is-it-possible-to-choose-for-a-pick-up-delivery-option": "<p>No, this is not possible. In order to provide the best quality products at affordable prices in a timely manner, we need flexibility in our production and shipping processes. The reason for this is because we work with many production locations across Europe. </p><p>When your order is placed, we work to determine the optimal production location and shipping carrier to get your order to you as efficiently as possible. Locking into set pick-up points would limit our ability to adapt to changing circumstances, suppliers and carriers, to provide you the best value.</p>",
"is-my-order-guaranteed-to-be-delivered-on-the-chosen-date": "<p>Besides unforeseen circumstances on the carrier's side, 98% of our orders are delivered on time.</p><p><strong>Please note:</strong> Any delays in the production process are not included in this. For orders to go into production, the design has to be uploaded and approved before the deadline shown at the bottom of the page when ordering.</p>",
"managing-users-of-company-account": "<h3>Users overview</h3><p>You can see all users in your company account on the “Manage users” page in My account. In the overview, you will see all invited and active users. You can also invite new users and remove users on this page. </p><ul><li>If the user has been invited, their status will be “Invited”.</li><li>If the user has accepted the invitation and joined the company account, their status will be “Active”.</li><li>If the user has rejected the invitation, their status will be “Rejected”.</li></ul><h3>Inviting new users</h3><p>To start collaborating, invite new users to join your company account. To do so, go to the “Manage users” page in My account. </p><p>To invite a user, you need to provide their email address, and first and last name. Invited users will receive an invitation via email. The invitation expires after 96 hours, after which you can send the user a new invitation if needed. Once the invitation is successfully sent, you will receive a confirmation email from us. </p><p>Once a new user is invited and receives an email with the invitation, they can decide to accept it or reject it. If they accept the invitation, the user will be redirected to the company account page on my account. If the user does not have a HelloPrint account yet, they will need to create one before accepting the invitation. </p><p>Once a new user joins your company account, they will be able to see all orders placed in the company account and access the shared address book and invoices. They will also get the rights to add users to the company account, set a contact person, and edit or delete the company account.</p><h3>Deleting users</h3><p>If you would like to remove any users from the company account, you can do so on the “Manage users” page in My account. Click on the “Delete” icon next to the user you want to delete. </p><p>If a user is deleted, they will lose access to the company account details and shared order history. Users will keep their Helloprint account and the history of orders placed by them (including the orders they placed as part of the company account).</p><p>The VIP level of the company account will be affected when users are deleted, as the order history of those users won’t be accounted towards the annual print spend of the company account.</p>",
"my-order-arrived-incomplete-what-should-i-do": "<p>It's possible that another package is still on the way. </p><p>We recommend checking the shipping status of your order in <a href=\"#my-account\">Your Account</a>. If you don't see any additional package on the way, please fill out the complaint form <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a>. We will investigate the issue as soon as possible.</p>",
"my-order-has-been-delivered-damaged-what-should-i-do": "<p>Firstly, we're very sorry to hear that your order has arrived damaged.</p><p>The best thing to do is to fill out our complaint form <a href=\"#new2contactform\">here</a>. Make sure to add clear pictures or a video of the damage, the box/packaging and the shipping label. This way, we can solve it for you right away.</p>",
"my-payment-has-failed-what-should-i-do": "<p>We recommend checking if the amount has already been debited from your account. If not, we recommend placing the order again. If your payment fails a second time, please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact</a> our print experts.</p>",
"my-track-and-trace-code-is-not-working-what-can-i-do": "<p>Once your order has been shipped, you will receive an email with the tracking link to follow your order. Did you open this link and can't find your package? Don't panic! This is probably due to the carrier not scanning your package yet. If that is the case, the tracking link will be active the next day</p><p>If by the following day, the link is still not active, please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and we can investigate the issue for you.</p>",
"what-are-cmyk-colours": "<p>Cyan, magenta, yellow, and black (CMYK) are the inks typically used for printing. When they are combined, they create a dark colour, which is usually black. In printed artwork, the ink is usually applied to the material in layers of different colours, and the combination of these colours creates a full-color image.</p>",
"what-are-our-bank-details": "<p>If you want to pay manually, please remember to mention your customer ID number in the payment description.</p><p>Account name: Helloprint </p><p>Account number: 20015209 </p><p>IBAN: NL12AINH2268349286</p><p>VAT Registration Number: IE3469492VH </p><p>Sort Code: 40-62-52</p>",
"what-are-pantone-colours": "<p>The Pantone company has defined more than 2,100 colours that each have their own unique number. These numbers guarantee that all colours anywhere in the world are exactly the same, making Pantone colours particularly well-suited for corporate logos and house styles.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Pantone colours are also called PMS colours.</p>",
"what-are-rgb-colours": "<p>Colours are created by combining different light colours. When red, green, and blue (RGB) are combined, they create white light. In digital artwork, each pixel is composed of red, green, and blue light, and combining these three colours creates a colourful and vibrant image.</p>",
"what-are-safety-margins": "<p>Safety margins refer to the space between the printed piece's edge and the design's outermost visible elements. This space is a buffer zone that ensures the design looks visually balanced and consistent. If essential elements, such as text or logos, are too close to the edge of the printed material, they may get cut off or look visually unbalanced.</p><p>In addition to safety margins, printing templates may include other guides for folding lines, perforation lines, non-printable areas, non-visible areas or the location where glue is applied.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-2e82f3a5f3/c12a211db133bc60d87909996849f2eb/2e82f3a5f3-screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-19-28-xsm.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-19-28-xsm.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"what-are-the-pre-flight-notes-on-my-proof": "<p>When we generate your proof we check your file automatically, and everything we found is listed beside the proof. Notes come in two kinds:</p><ul><li><strong>Auto-applied</strong> — safe fixes we already made: RGB converted to CMYK, bleed extended, fonts embedded. Nothing to do; just good to know.</li><li><strong>Check this</strong> — things only you can judge: a low-resolution image, text close to the trim line. Look at each one on the proof; want to fix something? Choose <strong>Upload new artwork</strong>.</li></ul><p>Approving the proof means you're happy with the file <em>including</em> these notes — so give them a minute before you approve. And once you approve, that's final: your file goes straight to production and can't be changed afterwards.</p>",
"what-can-i-do-in-my-account": "<p>My Account is your home base after you order — track and manage every order, download invoices, and keep your details and company settings in one place. Here's what's inside:</p><ul><li><strong>Orders</strong> — live status, parcel tracking, proof approval, cancellations and reorders.</li><li><strong>Invoices</strong> — every invoice and credit note as PDF.</li><li><strong>Addresses</strong> — your address book and default shipping address.</li><li><strong>Details &amp; settings</strong> — password, email preferences, invoice email.</li><li><strong>Company account</strong> — colleagues, VAT details, Pay on Invoice.</li></ul><p>Can't sign in? <a href=\"help-article.html?q=how-do-i-reset-my-password\">Here's how to get back in</a>.</p>",
"what-colour-profile-do-i-need-to-use-for-my-design": "<p>We use FOGRA39 (ISO Coated V2) for coated products and FOGRA47 (ISO Uncoated V2) for uncoated products. If you are unsure of the colour mode of your file or how to prepare this in your file, don't worry, we will always convert this for you in our art work check process.</p>",
"what-does-it-mean-when-you-pay-extra-for-turnaround-time": "<p>When you pay extra for your turnaround, this actually refers to a faster production time. We produce all orders on time, but unfortunately we cannot always guarantee that delivery will be on time where external factors are involved.</p><p>At HelloPrint, we’re lucky to have a large international network of production facilities. We work closely with a selection of delivery companies to make sure we can provide the best product, price and service possible.</p>",
"what-does-the-status-assigned-to-my-order-mean": "<p>Your order moves through five simple stages. Here's what each one means:</p><ul><li><strong>Submitted</strong> — we've received your order.</li><li><strong>Artwork</strong> — we're checking your files and preparing your proof. We'll let you know if we need anything from you, or once your proof is ready to approve.</li><li><strong>Production</strong> — your approved files are being prepared and printed.</li><li><strong>Shipped</strong> — your order is on its way, and you'll have a tracking link to follow it.</li><li><strong>Delivered</strong> — your order has arrived.</li></ul><p>Two other states can appear alongside these:</p><ul><li><strong>On hold</strong> — occasionally an order pauses, for example if we need something from you. We'll show what's holding it up and what's needed to continue.</li><li><strong>Cancelled</strong> — the order, or an item in it, has been cancelled.</li></ul>",
"what-file-type-should-i-use-when-uploading-my-design": "<p><strong>The preferred format for print design is PDF,</strong> as it preserves design elements, colours, and resolution without compromising quality. </p><p>No need to sweat it if you've already handed in a different file format! We can still work with most of those too. Different file types have unique properties that make them ideal for specific purposes. For example, PDF files are print-ready and suitable for complex documents with multiple pages, while EPS files are perfect for vector logos and graphics. </p><p><strong>Common file formats (JPG, PNG, PDF):</strong> JPG and PNG files are commonly used for web graphics but can be used for print materials if they have a high enough resolution. PDF files are the industry standard for print-ready documents. Do you have a Word file? Please save this as a pdf before submitting. </p><p><strong>Specialised file formats (EPS, AI, INDD):</strong> EPS files are suitable for vector graphics, while AI files are preferred for complex designs. INDD files are used in desktop publishing and are suitable for multi-page documents.</p><p><strong>Design Tools:</strong> We support the above mentioned file formats from design tools such as, Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Sketch, QuarkXPress etc...</p>",
"what-happens-if-i-miss-my-proof-approval-deadline": "<p>Nothing dramatic. Your order isn't cancelled, and we never approve on your behalf — your file only prints when <strong>you</strong> approve it.</p><p>The one thing that changes is your delivery date: it moves back, usually by one working day, and keeps moving until you approve. Your order page shows both the original and the updated delivery date, plus the new deadline that locks it in.</p>",
"what-happens-when-the-delivery-attempts-were-unsuccessful": "<p>In the event that the courier is unable to deliver your order, it will be returned to one of our depots. There are various reasons why the courier may face difficulties in delivering the order. The main reasons are unavailability upon delivery or an error in the address or incorrect sorting or routing by the carrier. </p><p>Once a returned order has reached our depot, we will always send a message by email to notify you of this. If you have received this message, it is important to respond to it as soon as possible. We try to store the package for as long as possible. However, after seven days, the package will be disposed. By responding to the message, we can start a resending process and prevent this from happening. </p><p>In cases of incorrect shipping address or unavailability upon delivery we charge a delivery fee of €15 excluding VAT . This price covers the costs of storage at the depot, processing the package and resending it. </p><p><strong>Please note:</strong> Check your shipping address with care, to prevent the order from being returned to us again.</p>",
"what-is-a-company-account": "<p>With a company account, you can invite your colleagues to collaborate on ordering at HelloPrint. With a company account, you and your colleagues can place orders, approve artwork, and share invoices. </p><ul><li>Want to give your designer access to upload and approve designs for your orders?</li><li>Need to share invoices for your orders with your colleagues from accounting?</li><li>Going on leave and planning to hand over your orders to a colleague?</li></ul><p>Use our company account feature to share the access and start the collaboration.</p>",
"what-is-a-digital-proof": "<h4><strong>First things first - what is a digital proof?</strong></h4><p>Well, the digital proof is a preview of your print ready design that will be sent to production. </p><p>After uploading your file to the order, you may receive a digital proof right away, automatically created by our system. If this is the case, you will be given the choice to approve it directly and send it to production, or have a digital proof created by our artwork specialists. Either way, remember to only approve your digital proof once you’re 100% happy with the design!</p><p><strong>TIP:</strong> Take an extra look at the proof if you have received warnings from our artwork team. Warnings mean that something has been changed in your file or that the file is not 100% suitable.</p><p>We show proofs sometimes without bleed and sometimes with bleed. </p><ul><li>Do you see your proof <strong>WITH</strong> cut marks? Then the proof is shown <strong>WITH</strong> bleed. </li><li>Do you see your proof <strong>WITHOUT</strong> cutting marks? Then the proof is shown <strong>WITHOUT</strong> bleed.</li></ul><h4></h4>",
"what-is-and-what-is-not-included-in-a-premium-deluxe-artwork-check": "<p>If you select the Premium Artwork Check, this means that:</p><ul><li>We will do basic resolution, size and colour checks.</li><li>Your files will be converted into a verified PDF. </li><li>You will receive a print proof (digital proof) before production.</li></ul><p>If you select the Deluxe Artwork Check, it means that:</p><ul><li>We will do everything that is included in the premium design check.</li><li>In addition, one of our experts will review your design.</li><li>Your files will be optimised using AI (if possible).</li></ul><p>However, we're never able to check:</p><ul><li>Spelling mistakes.</li><li>Overprint.</li></ul>",
"what-is-bleed-and-do-i-need-it-in-my-design": "<p>Bleed refers to the area of an image or design that extends beyond the finished size of the printed piece. When a design includes bleed, the ink will be printed to the edge of the material and then trimmed down to the final size.</p><p>Bleeding is necessary in your design because it allows slight variations in the trimming process and ensures no white borders around the edge of the finished piece.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-b2b019b7a5/13f9fb1b76c4f8b4f5792c145a96a8ff/b2b019b7a5-screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-23-19-rjw.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-04-25-20at-2012-23-19-rjw.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"what-is-dpi": "<p>DPI (dots per inch) refers to the physical density of the dots or ink droplets used to create a printed image. The higher the DPI, the more dots per inch and the sharper and more precise the printed image.</p>",
"what-is-ink-absorption": "<p>The amount of ink that is printed on material (paper, cardboard, metal, etc.) is measured by adding the total percentages of each CMYK ink used. As a general rule, if more than 300% coverage is used, it is likely that not all of the ink will be absorbed and smudging will occur.</p><p>For example, a black tone with 91% Cyan, 79% Magenta, 62% Yellow and 97% Black is equivalent to 329% coverage. It is strongly recommended to reduce the mix so as not to exceed 300%.</p>",
"what-is-overprint": "<p>Imagine you have a red circle and a yellow square. If you overprint them, the area where they overlap might appear orange. It's like stacking transparent colors to see what new color you get where they intersect.</p><p>Overprinting is often used in graphic design and printing to achieve specific color blends and effects in the final printed material. However, if that is not what you are trying to acchieve, it's crucial to ensure that overprinting is done correctly to avoid unwanted results.</p><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-78840ac135/52eeda342e992cf5be07c580b7e9f808/78840ac135-overprint-20example-20helloprint-w4u.png\" alt=\"overprint-20example-20helloprint-w4u.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"what-is-resolution": "<p>Resolution is the number of pixels, or picture elements, that make up an image. It determines the amount of detail that can be seen in an image and is measured in terms of the total number of pixels, both horizontally and vertically. A higher resolution means more pixels and finer detail, while a lower resolution means fewer pixels and less detail.</p>",
"what-is-secured-delivery": "<p>Secured Delivery is an optional paid add-on you can choose at checkout.</p><p>If your order arrives after the latest promised delivery date, we'll refund 20% of the order value. It's a refund promise for late delivery — it doesn't change how your parcel is handled, and it isn't a guarantee against loss or damage.</p><p>To claim, contact us via our <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact form</a> and we'll look into it for you.</p>",
"what-is-the-biggest-file-size-i-can-upload": "<p>Our standard ordering process supports file uploads up to 250MB. For larger files, we offer an alternative uploader that can handle files up to 1GB.</p>",
"what-is-the-difference-between-a-digital-or-print-ready-design-file": "<p>It's essential to understand the difference between digital and print-ready design files. A digital file’s purpose is to be viewed on a screen. These files are typically saved in a lower resolution and use RGB colours. On the other hand, a print-ready file is optimised for printing. They are typically saved in a higher resolution and usually contain CMYK colours.</p>",
"what-is-the-difference-between-raster-and-vectors": "<p>We can categorise design files into two main types: raster and vector. Raster files comprise pixels, while vector files comprise mathematical equations that create shapes and lines. </p><p>Raster files are best for images and photographs. In contrast, vector files are better for logos, icons, and other designs that require crisp lines and shapes. In addition, vector files can be scaled up or down without losing quality, while raster files can become pixelated if they are enlarged too much.</p>",
"what-is-the-difference-between-rgb-and-cmyk": "<p>When converting an RGB image to CMYK, it is essential to understand that the colours will differ. This is because the range of colours that CMYK can produce is smaller than the range of colours that RGB can produce. </p><p>To give an example, consider a bright green colour created using RGB. When converting the image to CMYK, the colour may appear more muted and darker because it is created by mixing inks (mostly cyan and yellow). Mixing ink will always result in a darker or more muted colour, as opposed to mixing light, which results in a lighter colour.</p>",
"what-is-the-difference-between-rich-black-and-100-black": "<p>While a rich black mix allows printing a deeper and darker black colour, it's not always recommended for text, particularly smaller fonts. In addition, using a mixture of different ink colours to create rich black text can result in a less legible and blurry result, making it harder to read and understand.</p><p>In most cases, it's recommended to use 100% black ink for text and reserve rich black for larger objects such as backgrounds.</p>",
"what-is-the-status-of-my-complaint": "<p>You can track anything you've reported under My Account → Support. Open the case to see its current status and our latest reply — and we'll email you whenever there's an update.</p>",
"what-should-i-do-if-my-package-hasn-t-been-delivered": "<p>Please check the track and trace information sent via email for the latest delivery status.</p><p>It is possible that the delivery driver may have experienced a delay. Normally, the order will be delivered on the next working day. However, if there is a delay of more than two working days, we recommend <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contacting</a> our print experts.</p>",
"what-will-happen-if-i-m-not-at-the-delivery-address": "<p>If you’re not at home when your order is delivered, carriers will either:</p><ol><li>Leave your order in a safe place (on your property or with a neighbour)</li><li>Take it back to the depot</li><li>Try to deliver it on the next business day</li><li>Leave it at a local drop-off point</li></ol><p>You can use the track and trace information to check this.</p>",
"when-do-i-get-free-shipping": "<p>Want to save on shipping costs? At HelloPrint we make that easy for you. Spend over 60 pounds excluding VAT and the shipping is on the house. Simply add your favourite business cards, flyers or stationery to your cart and once the total amount reaches 60 pounds excluding VAT, shipping becomes free.</p><p>The shipping fees might differ, depending on which product and amounts you are ordering.</p><p><strong>Please note:</strong> this offer does not apply to products of custom size, such as banners and custom posters, custom stickers etc.</p>",
"when-do-i-upload-my-artwork": "<h2>If you would like to upload your artwork before payment:</h2><ol><li>Add the product you would like to order to your cart.</li><li> Proceed to the payment page.</li><li>Select \"Continue to Pay later, upload my artwork first\".</li><li>Proceed to upload your artwork.</li></ol><h2><strong>If you would like to pay before uploading your artwork:</strong></h2><ol><li> Add the product you would like to order to your cart. </li><li>Proceed to the payment page.</li><li>Select any of the payment options to directly pay for your order (for more information about the payment options, check out <a href=\"#help-article\">this article</a>). </li><li>Proceed to upload your artwork.</li></ol><p>Once your order is in production, you can't make any changes to your artwork, so please make sure to thoroughly check everything before approving.</p>",
"when-will-i-receive-my-invoice": "<p>Once your order status shows \"Your order has been shipped\", we’ll send you the invoice by email. You can also access and download your invoice in <a href=\"#my-account\">My Account</a>. </p><p>Just to remind you, we’ll never send any physical documents related to your order upon delivery.</p>",
"where-can-i-find-my-credit-invoice": "<p>To access your (credit) invoices, simply go to the left-hand menu in <a href=\"#my-account\">your account</a> and select the 'invoices' section. You will also receive a digital copy of your credit invoice by email.</p>",
"where-can-i-find-my-order-status": "<p>To easily track the status of your order, follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Click on your name located in the upper right corner of the screen to reveal a dropdown menu.</li><li>From the dropdown menu, select \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" to access your order history.</li><li>Your orders will be listed in chronological order, with the most recent ones displayed first. Look for the \"Status\" column to determine the current status of each order.</li></ol><p>For a more comprehensive view of a specific order, simply click on \"Order Details\" on the right side of the screen, adjacent to the desired order.\"</p>",
"where-can-i-find-the-design-guide": "<img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-1fcb612807/e07c5318bba39063602400ab63b386ba/1fcb612807-screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-15-vz4.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-15-vz4.png\" loading=\"lazy\">",
"where-can-i-find-the-templates-for-my-design": "<img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-d38861c37e/af3a066da79754aa2c7173f37a8c3122/d38861c37e-screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-15-aok.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-15-aok.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><img src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/wm1n7oady8a5/hcImg-6cdb591e2f/812974adafacb0de5f03c5a020ef6782/6cdb591e2f-screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-26-dz4.png\" alt=\"screenshot-202023-11-16-20at-2010-37-26-dz4.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><p><strong>please note:</strong></p><ul><li> For optimal results, we recommend using the template specific to the product you're designing. Despite similar dimensions across products, nuances in trim, bleed, and safety margins may exist.</li><li>Designing with our on-site Canva tool? No need for separate templates. Canva will guide you with the correct trim, bleed, and safety margins in the final steps as you hand in your artwork.</li></ul>",
"where-do-i-start-when-preparing-my-design-for-printing": "<p>Creating a print-ready design is exciting, but looking at the design specifications can look overwhelming. To get you started, this article will cover the basics for preparing your file for printing. </p><ol><li><strong>Start with checking the print specifications, guides and templates:</strong> Please note that specific printing requirements may vary for each product. You can download our guides and templates at the top of the product page. Following these specifications will ensure your design gets perfectly printed. </li><li><strong>Use high-quality images:</strong> Delivering high-resolution images and graphics in your file is essential. The standard quality for most commercial print and stationery is 300 dpi. Outdoor products and formats bigger than a meter must be at least 150 dpi. If you opted for solid colours or laser engraving, your file should be submitted as a vector graphic. </li><li><strong>Use CMYK colour mode:</strong> RGB colour mode is reserved for digital media and requires a conversion that may result in muted printed colours. By designing in CMYK, you ensure that your printed product closely matches your intended design. </li><li><strong>Adjust your design to fit the template:</strong> Resize and reposition the artwork to match the template's dimensions, layout, and orientation. Also, make sure your page count matches what you ordered and remember prices are shown per design. You will need to add units individually to your cart for multiple designs. </li><li><strong>Verify and adjust bleed and margins when applicable:</strong> A correct bleed and safety margin ensures that no essential elements are cut off and no white lines appear after trimming. </li><li><strong>Manage your fonts, texts and small elements:</strong> We recommend embedding or outlining the fonts on your design to avoid any issues. If your design contains small black text, make sure it is 100 % black (Cyan: 0, Magenta: 0, Yellow: 0, Black: 100). Ensure thin lines and small text meet the minimum size requirements for legibility in the final product. Note that we don't check spelling or typographical errors. </li><li><strong>Delete the template layers:</strong> Always delete any template layers before exporting your file. These layers are meant to guide your design process and should not be included in the final print. </li><li><strong>Export to PDF:</strong> The best approach is exporting to print-ready PDF format. If you already have a design, no worries; we accept other file formats, including JPEG, PNG, or EPS. For instance, high-resolution JPEGs are an excellent option for photographic content.</li></ol>",
"where-will-they-cut-my-final-product": "<p>We will know where to cut thanks to crop marks.</p><p>Crop marks are lines added to the artwork's edges to indicate where the piece will be trimmed after printing. These marks show the printer where to cut the material to achieve the desired finished size.</p>",
"which-payment-options-do-i-have": "<p>You can pay securely with:</p><ul><li>Credit or debit card</li><li>PayPal</li><li>Bank transfer (SEPA)</li><li><strong>Pay on Invoice</strong> — for approved business customers. (<a href=\"#new2contactform\">Check if you're eligible</a>)</li></ul><p>The exact options you see at checkout depend on your country — local methods like iDEAL or Bancontact appear automatically wherever they're available.</p><p>One thing to know about bank transfer: we start production planning once your payment arrives, so on a tight deadline a card or another instant method is the faster choice. Every payment is processed securely.</p>",
"why-can-t-i-make-any-modifications-to-my-order-once-it-has-gone-into-production": "<p>It is very important to take extra care before you approve the proof. If you have chosen to send your files directly to our production site, you should also have received a warning message.</p>",
"why-did-i-receive-a-payment-reminder": "<p>We send you a payment reminder if we have not yet received a payment for your order. Please note that processing payments can take up to 3 business days. </p><p>When the payment term on the invoice has expired, we'll send a reminder via email once every two weeks. It is important to pay on time, otherwise you run the risk of incurring additional costs. </p><p>Have you already paid for the order? Please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and send us your proof of payment for your payment. We can then investigate and resolve the issue for you.</p>",
"why-did-the-delivery-date-change-since-i-placed-the-order": "<p>The delivery date shown on the order might sometimes vary from the product page due to various factors.</p><ol><li><strong>Delivery Window:</strong> On the product page, we display a date range from the earliest to the latest possible delivery. This longer window accounts for any potential delays in production or shipping, which are pre-calculated. The date shown on your order might reflect the latest possible delivery date, so please check your track and trace once the order has been dispatched for the most accurate delivery information.</li><li><strong>Missed Production Deadline:</strong> We display a daily deadline on the product page for uploading and approving your files. If the print-ready proof is not approved before this deadline, the delivery date will shift by one working day.</li><li><strong>Delays Due to Stock, Shipping or File Issues:</strong> Even though we deliver 95% of our orders in time, unforeseen delays may also occur due to stock shortages, shipping or issues with your print file. Please check your inbox, as we may have already sent an email regarding the issue. If not, contact us, and we'll assist you further.</li></ol>",
"why-do-i-need-to-pay-an-extra-charge-if-i-choose-pay-on-invoice": "<p>For the payment option 'Pay on invoice', we are asking for an extra charge of 2% of the order amount (with a minimum charge of 1.99€), as invoicing requires more administrative work than instant electronic payments.</p>",
"why-do-i-need-to-pay-for-faster-delivery": "<p>To ensure your order is delivered faster, your order needs to be printed / produced earlier. Therefore you pay extra for priority on the production line. </p><p><em>Note that delivery on the chosen date cannot always be guaranteed due to unexpected circumstances at the carrier, such as busy delivery schedules. We are dependent on our carriers and the reliability of delivery services can differ.</em></p>",
"why-does-my-canva-design-look-so-blurry": "<p>If your design looks blurry or pixelated, there are two common factors that could cause this. </p><p>- Using low quality images can result in blurry or pixelated images. Where possible, upload only high quality images in 300 DPI.</p><p>- Have you used filters? Some filters have a ‘softening’ effect when applied to an image or design. Simply remove the filter and see if the quality improves without it.</p>",
"why-does-my-print-look-different-from-my-screen": "<p>Screens mix light (RGB); printing mixes ink (CMYK) — which is why printing works in CMYK: it's the four-ink set that reproduces colour consistently on paper, the same way on every press. Some bright screen colours — vivid greens, electric blues — simply can't be mixed in ink, so they print slightly more muted. That's physics, not a printing error.</p><p>What happens with your file at HelloPrint: if it arrives in RGB we convert it automatically using the FOGRA standard printing profile, and flag the conversion in your proof's pre-flight notes — so you judge the result on the proof before approving.</p>",
"why-have-i-not-received-my-order-confirmation": "<p>It is possible that your order confirmation email ended up in your spam/junk folder, please check that folder first.</p><p>If you can't find an order confirmation there, please check if your order has been placed correctly by going to the \"<a href=\"#orders\">Orders</a>\" page in your account. If your order is listed there, there is no need to worry - we've received it. You can find the status of your order there. </p><p>If you don't see it listed after fifteen minutes, there may have been an error during the submission process. Please <a href=\"#new2contactform\">contact us</a> and we will happily assist you.</p>",
"why-is-my-discount-voucher-not-working": "<p>If the code is not expired and is applicable to all products in your cart, please contact us via <a href=\"#new2contactform\">this form</a>, and we will assist you with your issue.</p><p>Note that you can use only one discount code per purchase.</p>",
"why-is-my-order-on-hold": "<p>On hold means your order is paused. Open it under <strong>My Account → Orders</strong> — the banner there shows which of the two kinds applies:</p><ul><li><strong>Action needed (from you)</strong> — usually a proof waiting for approval, new artwork needed, or a delivery detail to confirm. The banner names the action; doing it releases the order immediately.</li><li><strong>On hold (with us)</strong> — we're resolving something on our side. No action needed from you, and if it affects your delivery date we'll contact you.</li></ul><p>Unsure? <a href=\"#new2contactform\">Contact us</a> with your order number.</p>",
"will-my-design-be-checked-for-overprint": "<p>Since this is a designer’s personal choice, we do not check or correct overprint on your designs.</p>"
};
